# Rust panic policy

## Library code (`src/`)

Allowed only: `todo!`, `unimplemented!`, `unreachable!`.

Forbidden: `panic!`, `unwrap`, `expect`, `unwrap_err`, `unwrap_unchecked`, `assert!`, `assert_eq!`, `assert_ne!`. Recoverable failure is `Result`.

```rust
// BAD
let id = map.get("id").unwrap();
panic!("missing id");

// GOOD
fn load_id(map: &Map) -> Result<&str, Error> {
    match map.get("id").and_then(Value::as_str) {
        Some(id) => Ok(id),
        None => Err(Error::rejected("missing id")),
    }
}

// GOOD — placeholder until the next stage implements it
todo!("functionality is not implemented")
```

## Tests (`tests/`, `#[cfg(test)]`)

`assert!`, `assert_eq!`, `assert_ne!`, `panic!`, `unwrap`, and `expect` are allowed.
